---
/**
 * The app, moving, at the head of `Screens`.
 *
 * It sits there and not under the hero: a full-width loop as the first thing
 * after the H1 read as a promo reel, and it showed the panes before the page
 * had said why any of them matter. Here the grant, the write gate and the log
 * have all been argued, and the captures that follow are the same window,
 * stopped. `make site-video` renders it from the `tour` entry in
 * apps/apple/Screenshots/screenshots.config.json, out of the same captures
 * `Screens.astro` and `SurfacePane.astro` show still, and writes it to
 * public/video — so it goes stale exactly when they do, and a fresh
 * `make screenshots` wants a `make site-video` after it. From public/ and not
 * astro:assets, which does nothing for video.
 *
 * `preload="none"` and no `autoplay`: the script below plays it only while it
 * is on screen, and not at all under reduced motion, where it stays on its
 * poster with the controls showing. The controls are the no-JS fallback too.
 * Muted because it has no sound to lose.
 *
 * Same 1120 CSS px column, plate styling and caption grid as the captures
 * below, so the window in it reads at the scale they do. A figure, not a
 * section: `Screens` places it in its column and owns the spacing.
 */
---

<figure id="tour" class="reveal m-0 scroll-mt-24">
  <video
    data-tour
    src="/video/tour.mp4"
    poster="/video/tour.jpg"
    width="1920"
    height="1080"
    muted
    loop
    playsinline
    controls
    preload="none"
    aria-label="A twenty-second loop of Cupertino's window: the sidebar of Apple apps under one grant, the activity log with a refused write, Notes with writes off and seven tools, and the on-device chat calling a Mail tool."
    class="mx-auto block h-auto w-full max-w-[1120px] rounded-[14px] border border-rule-2 shadow-[0_24px_60px_-34px_rgba(0,0,0,.9)]"
  >
  </video>
  <figcaption class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 gap-2 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.15fr] lg:gap-16">
    <h3 class="m-0 font-display text-[20px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-fg">
      Twenty seconds of it, moving.
    </h3>
    <p class="m-0 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.65] text-pretty text-fg-dim">
      Every Apple app behind one grant, the log as calls land, a surface with writes off, and the
      on-device chat calling a Mail tool. The captures below are the same window, stopped.
    </p>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
  // Plays the tour only while it is on screen. Reduced motion, or no
  // IntersectionObserver, leaves it as it rendered: paused, with controls.
  const tour = document.querySelector<HTMLVideoElement>("video[data-tour]");
  const still = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
  if (tour && !still && "IntersectionObserver" in window) {
    tour.controls = false;
    new IntersectionObserver(
      ([entry]) => {
        if (entry?.isIntersecting) void tour.play().catch(() => (tour.controls = true));
        else tour.pause();
      },
      { threshold: 0.4 },
    ).observe(tour);
  }
</script>
